<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  AmbientShrineGuardians.xml      UtinniPatches   SHRINE_GUARDIAN_BIOME_GATE_1
  ============================================================================
  Piece 4/4 of MECH_PRESENCE_ENFORCEMENT_1 — curate shrine CONTENTS on the
  eight biomes where the ratified ANCIENT column allows ancient dangers but
  the AMBIENT column bans mechanoids
  (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/mechanoid_biome_presence_draft.md).

  The full reasoning — which resolver actually decides guardian and loot, why
  the item spec's "Harmony postfix on SymbolResolver_AncientTemple" is the
  wrong target, what is substituted on those eight rows, and every judgment
  call made — lives in ONE place, the header of
  Source/AmbientShrineGuardians.cs. Read that; it is not repeated here.

  WHY NO HARMONY. Core's RuleDef Interior_AncientTemple
  (Data/Core/Defs/RuleDefs/Rules_Interior.xml:20-28) carries its resolver as
  `<li Class="SymbolResolver_Interior_AncientTemple">` inside a plain
  `List<SymbolResolver>` field (RuleDef.cs) with no LoadDataFromXmlCustom
  anywhere in the chain, and BaseGen.Resolve walks that list by reference —
  so setting the Class attribute to our subclass is the whole patch. Same
  no-Harmony, plain-subclass shape as Patches/GeothermalDensityField.xml.
  The `<minRectSize>(1, 1)</minRectSize>` child on that li is untouched:
  PatchOperationAttributeSet rewrites only the attribute.

  SAFETY. Interior_AncientTemple is Core and always present, but per this
  mod's convention (JawaResource_Scrapfields.xml's SAFETY note) the operation
  is wrapped in a PatchOperationConditional whose xpath is IDENTICAL to the
  inner operation's, so a future Core rename or restructure is a silent
  no-op — vanilla shrine contents everywhere — rather than a red error on
  every launch.

  ⛔ A clean patch-apply proves the xpath matched, nothing more. The biome
  gate itself is only proven by a quicktest map on one candidate biome; that
  is still OWED on SHRINE_GUARDIAN_BIOME_GATE_1.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/RuleDef[defName="Interior_AncientTemple"]/resolvers/li</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAttributeSet">
      <xpath>Defs/RuleDef[defName="Interior_AncientTemple"]/resolvers/li</xpath>
      <attribute>Class</attribute>
      <value>RimMandrake.Utinni.UtinniPatches.SymbolResolver_Interior_AncientTemple_AmbientDoctrine</value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
